-भूचक्रे तव यजनान्ययं न्यरौत्सीत् ॥ 18.2 ॥
-Word-by-word meaning: पापः अपि though wicked, क्षिति-तल-पालनाय for protecting the earth, वेनः Vena, पौर-आद्यैः by the citizens and others, उपनिहितः was installed as king, कठोर-वीर्यः of cruel prowess, सर्वेभ्यः to all people, निज-बलम् एव his own power alone, सम्प्रशंसन् praising highly, भूचक्रे on the earth, तव Your, यजनानि sacrifices offered to You, अयम् he, न्यरौत्सीत् stopped or prohibited
-Simple Meaning: Even though Vena was wicked and of cruel prowess, he was installed on the throne by the citizens and others for the protection of the earth. Praising his own power above all else, he completely prohibited all holy sacrifices offered to You throughout the earth.
