-स्वच्छन्दं सुरभितनूमदूदुहस्त्वम् ॥ 18.6 ॥
-Word-by-word meaning: भूयः further, ताम् her (the earth), निज-कुल-मुख्य-वत्स-युक्त्यैः with the leader of each group as the calf, देव-आद्यैः by the gods and others, समुचित-चारु-भाजनेषु in suitable beautiful vessels, अन्न-आदीनि food grains and other items, अभिलषितानि desired, यानी तानि whatever they were, स्वच्छन्दम् freely, सुरभि-तनूम् (the earth) in the form of Surabhi (the celestial cow), अदूदुहः त्वम् You milked
-Simple Meaning: Further, You made the earth yield like the celestial cow Surabhi. By having the gods, sages, and others in the form of calves from their own groups and bringing appropriate vessels, You allowed them to freely milk from the earth all the food grains and desired treasures they wished for.
