-रोगौघं प्रशमय वातगेहवासिन् ॥ 18.10 ॥
-Word-by-word meaning: विज्ञानम् supreme spiritual wisdom, सनक-मुख-उदितम् imparted by Sanaka and the other sages, दधानः bearing or absorbing, स्व-आत्मानम् Your true self, स्वयम् Himself, अगमः attained, वन-अन्त-सेवी dwelling in the deep forest, तत्-तादृक्-पृथु-वपुः ईश O Lord who took that magnificent form of King Prithu, सत्वरम् quickly, मे my, रोग-ओघम् multitude of diseases, प्रशमय relieve or cure, वात-गेह-वासिन् O Resident of Guruvayur
-Simple Meaning: Absorbing the divine spiritual wisdom imparted by Sanaka and the other sages, You retired to the deep forest and attained Your true divine nature. O Lord of Guruvayur, who incarnated in that glorious form of King Prithu, please quickly cure the multitude of diseases afflicting me.
